  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated HIV, Water and Sanitation Project- JOAC - Hopley</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In responding to the needs of the most vulnerable communities hit hard by HIV and AIDS , Mashambanzou , is reaching out to Hopley, a  community of displaced people in Harare&apos;s High Density suburbs following operation clean -up (Murambatsvina).
Tis project will focus at the orphans and vulnerable children , a majority of whom are living with the virus . They attend school at Tariro School, which means HOPE as this is meant to keep the hope in children alive. This project will add life to the children and their community as it will bring flush toilets and other sanitation facilities to the school. Borehole water and introducing a garden at the school for the benefit of the children both academically, and meeting their nutrition needs.
The aim of this project is to ensure there is improved water, sanitation and hygiene standards for the vulnerable community  in Hopley- Zimbabwe, especially children.</narrative>
  </description>
